01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:43,500
Citizenfour is a 2014 documentary film directed by Laura Poitras,
concerning Edward Snowden and the NSA spying scandal.

11
01:17:41,250 --> 01:17:47,250
The film had its US premiere on October 10, 2014, at the New York Film Festival and
its UK premiere on October 17, 2014, at the BFI London Film Festival.

12
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
The film features Snowden and Glenn Greenwald, and was co-produced by Poitras, Mathilde Bonnefoy,
and Dirk Wilutzky, with Steven Soderbergh and others serving as executive producers.

13
01:31:48,750 --> 01:31:54,750
Citizenfour received critical acclaim upon release, and was the recipient of numerous
accolades, including Best Documentary Feature at the 87th Academy Awards.

14
01:38:52,500 --> 01:38:58,500
This film is the third part to a 9/11 trilogy following My
Country, My Country (2006) and The Oath (2010).

15
01:45:56,250 --> 01:46:02,250
The film explores themes of biography, national security agency (nsa),
woman director, investigative journalism, whistleblower.
